AzamiOS licensing
=================

Copyright (c) 2021-2026, a0w-svg and contributors.

AzamiOS is made of two parts under two licenses, the same arrangement the
Linux kernel and its user space use:

The kernel — GPL-2.0-only
-------------------------

Everything outside userland/, tools/ and scripts/ — arch/, kernel/, drivers/,
fs/, hal/, include/ and the build files that produce kernel.elf — is
provided under the terms of the GNU General Public License version 2 only
(LICENSES/GPL-2.0.txt, also in the top-level LICENSE file).

This is what allows code from the Linux kernel, which is GPL-2.0-only, to be
used in AzamiOS: a kernel binary that contains it must be distributed under
the GPL, and so the kernel as a whole is licensed that way.

  NOTE: the kernel's license does not cover programs that use it through
  normal system calls. Running on AzamiOS, calling its system calls, and
  including its user-space API headers (include/azami/uapi/, marked
  "GPL-2.0-only WITH Linux-syscall-note") is normal use of the kernel and does
  not make a program a derived work of it. This is the same exception Linux
  makes; its SPDX text is in LICENSES/Linux-syscall-note.txt.

  Only version 2 of the GPL applies to the kernel, not later versions,
  unless a file states otherwise.

User space and build tooling — BSD-3-Clause
-------------------------------------------

userland/ (the C library, dynamic linker, libgame and applications), tools/
and scripts/ remain under the BSD 3-Clause License
(LICENSES/BSD-3-Clause.txt). BSD-3-Clause is compatible with the GPL, so
these parts can also be combined with the kernel's GPL code where needed,
while programs built against AzamiOS's C library are not required to be GPL.

Third-party files
-----------------

Files that carry their own license notice keep it. In particular:

  - arch/x86_64/boot/limine.h, derived from the Limine boot protocol header,
    and tools/limine/ (the Limine bootloader): 0BSD / BSD-2-Clause, see the
    notices in those files.
  - Software fetched and built by tools/linux/ (musl, BusyBox, Bash, GNU
    coreutils, ...): each under its upstream license; nothing of it is
    stored in this repository.
  - Code ported from the Linux kernel keeps its original copyright notices
    and SPDX-License-Identifier lines.

Per-file license identifiers
----------------------------

A file may state its license with an SPDX line, for example

    // SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-only
    /* SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-only WITH Linux-syscall-note */

A file without one is covered by the directory rules above.
